12. Communication Failures

Failures MAY include:

Delivery timeout
Invalid artifact
Contract violation
Unauthorized access
Version incompatibility
Duplicate message
Processing failure

Failures SHALL:

Preserve traceability.
Record diagnostic information.
Support retry where appropriate.
Prevent semantic corruption.

13. Communication Quality Attributes

Atlas communications SHALL be evaluated for:

Reliability
Availability
Latency
Scalability
Consistency
Durability
Integrity
Observability

Quality expectations SHALL be documented for each communication contract.

14. Conformance

An implementation conforms if it:

Uses canonical communication patterns.
Preserves Canonical Engineering Artifacts.
Maintains communication traceability.
Documents delivery guarantees.
Implements standardized message metadata.
15. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Semantic routing.
Adaptive communication strategies.
Multi-region communication.
Agent-to-agent negotiation.
Intelligent message prioritization.

Such extensions SHALL preserve the canonical communication semantics.